            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"N0Dfd70vKo3C16x22MllfNEwg8e\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-Yv1GdtdjwoZ3j2xEseolhPL9gJg\">Looking at the chart in more detail, the top concern for younger workers is having the chance to develop themselves, as 90% of them believe so, versus only around 40% of older workers agreeing. Promotion prospects and a relaxed work environment are the next two most important factors for workers under 30, being mentioned by 80% of them. By contrast, only half of the workers over 45 cite the former as a factor, and only a third of them bring up the latter.</div>\n</div>",
